<h1>Recordings</h1>
<p>
  The birds are recorded through glass, the theremin is played at a
  distance, and the pad is mostly a night thing. None of it is
  released. Recommended listening is anything where the horn goes
  somewhere and doesn't explain itself, played in the dark.
</p>

<h2>Heard in the lounge</h2>
<ul class="terms">
  <li class="terms__item">Pharaoh Sanders, with the lights off.</li>
  <li class="terms__item">
    Mulatu Astatke and the Ethiopian jazz of the 1970s, mid-afternoon.
  </li>
  <li class="terms__item">Alice Coltrane, when the weather turns.</li>
  <li class="terms__item">Sun Ra, for the long evenings.</li>
</ul>

<h2>In progress</h2>
<p>
  Nothing here is finished, and the Founder would like that understood
  as a position.
</p>
<ul class="terms">
  <li class="terms__item">
    <strong>Magpie, 6:12am.</strong> A field recording, through the
    glass. Eleven minutes. Still being listened to.
  </li>
  <li class="terms__item">
    <strong>Starlings, Gutter.</strong> A field recording. The tail is
    audible if you know to listen for it.
  </li>
  <li class="terms__item">
    <strong>Theremin Sketch, Hand Hovering.</strong> No contact
    required. The instrument that suits him best.
  </li>
  <li class="terms__item">
    <strong>Pad Study No. 4.</strong> Chaos pad, paws only. Not a
    mistake.
  </li>
  <li class="terms__item">
    <strong>Untitled (Door).</strong> Recorded the evening of the
    argument. Do with that what you will.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Collaborators</h2>
<p>
  The Club does not work alone. These are the colleagues whose work he
  respects, and who haven't been asked.
</p>

